{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772909438,"nonce":"9ObPJHSP+hwONhZilyTyJi2QstA=","title":"Sessions project column: .dotfiles and dotfiles shown as duplicate pills","message":"When agent-commit runs in the dotfiles repo (cwd=/Users/mll/.dotfiles) with a cold IssueScanner cache, resolveCanonicalRepoId cannot resolve the canonical repo_id and falls back to the raw basename. deriveRepoNameFromRepoId does not strip leading dots, so .dotfiles is stored verbatim. The migration-25 backfill creates a separate dotfiles entry (via basename + strip-dots). Result: two project pills for the same repo.\n\nFix: strip leading dots in deriveRepoNameFromRepoId. Add a migration to fix existing rows. UI dedup should also normalize before comparing.","files":null}]}